From 256fefc160e27c5adea839f44e8b4e016ce97335 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:45:44 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent: open an agent session in its own project's window

Opening a task from the Agent Tasks panel loaded its thread into the
window the panel lives in, whatever project the thread belongs to: a
thread of project A opened from window B showed up in B's agent panel,
under B, and nothing in the UI moved it back. 0035's open_task called
focus_panel::<AgentPanel> and open_thread_by_session on its own
workspace. The window resolution that made the tray link correct --
folders from the metadata row, workspace::open_paths, raise -- lived only
in crate zed (0024's handle_open_request and its private
agent_session_folders), out of reach of agent_tasks_panel. 0035's test
used one window whose project matched the thread, so it asserted the
defect as correct behaviour; 0024's routing had no test at all. Story 024.

Same function, second defect: open_task ran inside the row's click
listener, while AgentTasksPanel was being updated. With both panels in one
dock, focus_panel made the dock call set_active on the tasks panel and
GPUI panicked with "cannot update AgentTasksPanel while it is already
being updated". 0039 moved the panel's default to the bottom dock, which
hides it in the default layout but not in one the user chooses.

One router, in agent_ui. agent_ui::open_agent_session(session_id,
OpenAgentSessionOptions { cwd, fallback_window, tool_call_id },
app_state, cx) -> Task<Result<OpenedAgentSession { window, workspace }>>.
It lives in agent_ui because agent_ui already owns AgentPanel,
ThreadMetadataStore and open_thread_by_session and depends on workspace;
agent_tasks_panel and zed both depend on agent_ui, so the tray link and
the panel now share it. What it does:

  * folders: waits on ThreadMetadataStore::reload_task, reads the row
    (agent_session_folders, moved here from main.rs unchanged); a
    remote_connection row gives none, a missing row falls back to cwd;
  * window: the one whose visible folders equal the thread's exactly, as a
    set in any order (open_paths' MatchExact takes the best partial match
    and would add the missing folder to the user's window); otherwise a
    NEW window over exactly those folders (WorkspaceMatching::None,
    OpenMode::NewWindow); without folders, fallback_window or the active
    window;
  * a folder that no longer exists -- a removed git worktree, say -- is an
    Err naming it, never a silent open in the focused window;
  * AI disabled is an Err at once, before any window is opened;
  * awaits the window's panels task, raises the window before focusing
    the agent panel (focus_panel alone does not raise it on KDE), and
    waits for a late AgentPanel through Workspace's PanelAdded event, or
    for the window to close; a window whose panels loaded without one is
    an Err at once, never a fall back to another window;
  * returns only once the panel shows a loaded conversation for that
    session; a load error is an Err; both waits are bounded at 60 s.

Every Err names the session and the step that failed. tool_call_id is
reserved for story 023 (open at the task) and ignored here.

The tray link (zeo://agent?session=) calls it and logs an Err at WARN;
the session-less link is untouched. AgentTasksPanel::open_task keeps its
"Thread no longer exists" check, then spawns the router with its own
window as the fallback, so nothing touches the workspace from inside the
click listener. A failure sets the row's notice to the reason and logs
one WARN line with the session and task ids; success clears the notice.

Tests: agent_ui agent_session_router 11 (exact match in any order,
prefix-named and sub-folder windows never taking a thread, remote and
cwd fallbacks, new window instead of a partial match, missing folders,
AI disabled, a late or absent agent panel, a window closed mid-wait);
zed agent_session_route 1 (tray link from window B lands in A); the
agent_tasks_panel suite 103, with open_routing (from B the thread lands
in A, no window opens one, remote stays, a failure shows its reason, a
real click in a shared left dock does not panic) and route_agreement
(router and panel row agree on window, workspace and folders).
